-# Packet Plumber (working title)
+# Packet Plumber
+
+A top-down routing puzzle: you are the network engineer keeping the internet
+alive. Draw pipes between buildings and routers, route colored packets by
+type through QoS priority lanes, read the warning signs, and survive the
+streaming surge — or watch the Network Health meter empty into **Error 404**.
+
+**Engine:** Odin (`dev-2026-08` pin) + raylib 6.0 (`vendor:raylib`). The
+proven-fun Godot prototype is preserved at the `prototype-fun-gate` tag
+(removed from main in the Odin pivot, ruled 2026-08-08).
+
+## Build & play
+
+```bash
+odin run app            # play (dev)
+odin build app          # produce the binary
+odin test core          # the determinism/fairness contract tests
+```
+
+Mouse-only prototype: drag node→node to draw pipes (1/2/3 picks the tier),
+right-click a pipe to cycle its QoS priority, click a router to inspect
+ports/flows + set triage, click a pipe for demolish. Space pauses (pause-and-
+plan is a doctrine). `A` toggles the autopilot (the demo build plays itself).
+
+## The golden-image harness (the verification loop)
+
+```bash
+tools/harness.sh run            # replay all demos: T1 state hashes + T2 pixels
+tools/harness.sh run surge_basics
+tools/harness.sh save           # re-bless goldens (deliberate, PR-reviewed)
+tools/harness.sh replay surge_basics goldens/surge_basics.log.bin
+```
+
+- **T1** — per-tick FNV-1a-64 of the full canonical sim state (topology, ALL
+  in-flight packet internals, SLA, rng, events). Bit-exact, no GPU needed.
+- **T2** — pixel goldens via raylib 6.0's rlsw software renderer +
+  PLATFORM_MEMORY (built by `tools/build_raylib_sw.sh`): bit-exact across
+  machines, no display. On mismatch the harness writes an agent-readable diff
+  bundle (`goldens/_reports/<demo>/...` with diff.png + diff.json).
+
+Demos live in `demos/*.dem` (seeded scenarios + virtual-clock intent scripts
++ event/hash expectations); they play through the real Input → Command_Bus →
+core path, and the validated command stream IS the replayable action log
+(ODN-11).
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+core/      package core — the simulation (pure Odin, deterministic, headless)
+app/       package main — the game (raylib window/input/audio)
+app/run/   package run  — orchestration (driver, command bus, catalogs)
+app/render/ package render — the light-canvas view
+harness/   package main — the golden-image runner
+demos/     scripted scenarios (*.dem)
+data/      JSON catalogs (single source of balance/content)
+goldens/   T1 manifests + T2 pixel goldens (+ _reports on failure; gitignored)
+tools/     raylib-sw build, harness runner, lint gates
+```
+
+The architecture (`_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/architecture/odin-architecture-v1.md`)
+is the spec; `project-context.md` governs code conduct.
