+## Other findings
+
+Genuine problems noticed while tracing verification (not verification gaps themselves):
+
+- **`pick_dst` allocates two fresh dynamic arrays per packet spawn from the run
+  arena** (`core/flow.odin:367-384`; `delete` is a no-op on an arena). Measured:
+  ~96 bytes/spawn, ~4.9 MB over a 3100-tick surge run against the 16 MB run arena
+  (`app/run/run.odin:52`). Bounded in practice because every run gets a fresh arena
+  (win/lose caps run length), but it contradicts the "zero per-frame heap churn" claim
+  and the margin is ~3 runs' worth, not infinite.
+- **`TICK_SECONDS :: 0.1`** (`app/run/run.odin:11`) is unused, with a comment claiming
+  it is "derived from balance.logic_hz" — it isn't; `driver.tick_seconds` is.
